# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net15, WIFID=1, connsys_step=17, XNU_SECS=118: the pictures of Settings.
# Run 82 (rc.jobs.net14, logs/lancelot-connsys32.log) tried battery_test's "launch" and "open"
# (SpringBoardServices' SBSLaunchApplicationWithIdentifier and SBSOpenSensitiveURLAndUnlock) and got
# nothing: battery_test is unsigned here (no ldid in the build), so SpringBoard will not do either for
# it. Its two pictures are both the home screen -- and that is what says where Settings is: the last
# row of the first page has Maps, Health, Wallet, Settings, so the icon is at 0.875 0.71 of the screen
# (the tap at 0.615 0.71 of run 80 opened Wallet, the icon beside it). The Wi-Fi row of Settings' list
# is the second one, about 0.245 down (Airplane Mode is the 0.209th, rows are 44 points at 812).
#
# The network is brought up first so the pane has something to show; fbwait waits for the first swap
# (~81 s) and 16 s more for the first real frame. fbgrab is the last thing: the JPEG goes to the
# console in base64 and the log keeps the last ~261 KB. XNU_SECS=118 ends the run about 6 s after the
# second picture.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fetch http://example.com/ 20
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.875 0.71
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 12
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log settings 300 0.4
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.245
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 8
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log wifi 300 0.4